    /* How many columns a code point takes. Code in edi, the variant in rsi:
       UNICODE_WIDTH_TERMINAL (0) or UNICODE_WIDTH_WCWIDTH (1).

       Two compares go first, as they did in term.c: below U+0300 everything
       is one column but wc's C1 controls, which setb and the variant make
       nought; and U+3250-A48C and the Hangul syllables, the ideographs most
       of a wide stream is, are two for both readers. Everything else under
       U+40000 is unicode_width_tab's three loads -- block, leaf offset,
       leaf byte -- and a shift of (c & 1) * 4 + variant * 2. Past U+3FFFF
       the tag and variation selector slice at U+E0000 is looked up from
       index 0x40000, and the rest are one column for the terminal and, for
       wc, one on the private use planes but for their last two code points
       and nought on every unassigned plane. Past U+10FFFF both are one, as
       the C was. No vector state: the kernel's terminal calls this. */
