    /* Deflate primary-table decode. job (88 bytes): bits, bit count <64,
       input cursor/limit, output cursor/limit, valid history before output,
       literal[512], distance[64], length info[29], distance info[30]. Cells
       are symbol | (nbits<<9), zero for longer/missing codes. Info cells are
       base | (extra<<16), the RFC 1951 constants. Tables are naturally aligned.
       Input/output cursors must be ordered within valid spans; input lookahead
       never crosses limit. Output has a valid 32 KiB history prefix, of which
       at least min(history,32768) bytes are initialized. The kernel stops with
       a token unconsumed on long codes, EOB, invalid distances, or short spans.
       Checksums/framing and that exact tail belong to the caller. Small match
       periods double up to a word before wide copying; RV peels only when the
       distance preserves alignment, otherwise it keeps the exact byte loop. */
