    // The hash block cores: see the x86_64 block for the contract, the
    // renamed registers and the lazy feature question. RV64IMAFD has no
    // rotate, so each is a shift pair, and no word is loaded from an
    // address not proven aligned.
    // md5_blocks: the sixteen words and the four chaining values live in
    // registers for the whole call, the constants come from a table held
    // in s9, and each round renames the register that took the sum as b.
    // A block at a doubleword-aligned address loads as eight ld with the
    // high half shifted down; any other address builds each word from bytes.
